OAKLAND TECH DIGEST
Friday, September 11, 2026

Hi neighbors,

Startup Week has dates, the library has a panel, and the Foundry needs hands on Saturday the 19th. Here is the next two weeks.

THIS WEEK
- Oakland Startup Week is set for October 12 to 16, spread across Uptown, Old Oakland, and Jack London Square. The organizers are taking session proposals until September 25: https://oaklandtechdigest.org/startup-week
- Ninth Street Commons, a new coworking space in Old Oakland with a shared electronics bench, opens October 1. Founding memberships are half price through the end of September.

COMING UP
- Tue Sep 15, 6:00pm | "AI in the trades" panel, Oakland Public Library main branch. An electrician, a machinist, and a community-college instructor on what the tools are actually doing on job sites. Free. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/trades-sep15
- Thu Sep 17, 12:00pm | Women Founders Lunch, Old Oakland. Monthly, informal, bring a question. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/wfl-sep17
- Sat Sep 19, 10:00am | Volunteer build day at Fifth Street Foundry. Help move the shop into the new bay; lunch provided; no skills required. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/foundry-sep19
- Tue Sep 22, 6:00pm | Uptown Hardware Meetup. Details next issue.

COMMUNITY
- The East Bay Robotics Demo Night drew about 120 people last week; the winning team built a shelf-scanning robot out of a modified floor cleaner. Photos: https://oaklandtechdigest.org/p/robots-sep10
- A reader-run study group on industrial control systems meets Wednesdays at 7pm at the Foundry; newcomers welcome.

JOBS BOARD
- Mechanical engineer, Emeryville (climate hardware)
- Operations lead, Ninth Street Commons
- Field technician, Oakland (building-sensor installer)
Post a job: https://oaklandtechdigest.org/jobs

See you around the lake,
Desmond

